{
  "text": "So I have had the Apple Vision Pro on my face for twenty-four hours. The eye tracking feels like telepathy. You look at an icon, tap your fingers together in your lap, and it instantly responds. The passthrough video is sharp enough to read your phone screen through the headset. However, you definitely feel the weight on your cheekbones after forty minutes. And having a battery pack tethered to your hip is an undeniable compromise.",
